+# Architecture Decision Desk verification
+
+Candidate source: existing report CLI and synthetic consultant-brief fixture at `d2bf5e778d5c4f08a1196551d32b90acf4244bec`, plus the generated browser projection and local editor in this change.
+
+On 21 October 2026, the integration verifier ran the existing 21 report tests and five browser projection contracts: 26 passed. Independent local browser verification used Playwright 1.58.2 with test-only Chromium 147.0.7727.0, at 320, 390, 768 and 1440 CSS pixels. The bundled Playwright browser download was unavailable in that environment; the alternative runtime was installed separately and is not a product dependency.
+
+Observed checks: no horizontal page overflow; markup-like input rendered literally; malformed imports preserved current edits; incoming decisions required review and supported cancellation; incomplete working JSON could be downloaded and reopened for repair; validated Markdown matched the canonical CLI semantics; control IDs were unique; no page errors, external requests, localStorage entries or sessionStorage entries occurred in the exercised journey.
+
+The browser core is a generated projection. `node scripts/build-browser-kit.mjs --check` must pass before release. Canonical report behavior remains in `scripts/architecture-review.mjs`; do not edit `web/review-core.js` directly.
+
+Scope: synthetic local verification only. This tool does not execute an agent, enforce a trust boundary, authenticate declared evidence, stop provider spend or establish an accepted customer result. Keyboard/reflow spot checks are not a comprehensive assistive-technology certification. No external-buyer trial or merchant fulfillment was run.
+
+Recovery: save working JSON before closing or replacing a decision. Invalid/incomplete saved files can be opened in the repair editor and corrected before applying. Keep the CLI and prior JSON/Markdown files as the portable fallback. To roll back this browser candidate, remove its link and serve the prior public worksheet/CLI; existing source formats are unchanged.
